WEBVTT

00:00:09,650 --> 00:00:15,490
Would any inflammation still present after the surgery show up in a pet scale?

00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:24,610
The answer that is yes and no. So if they won't do a pet scan,

00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:34,770
within at least at least 30 days after surgery, and some practitioners won't do it for three

00:00:34,770 --> 00:00:41,570
months after surgery, because when your body is healing from something, yes, you're going to have

00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:50,690
an increased metabolic activity, and you can show up. There can be some increase in

00:00:52,290 --> 00:00:58,610
pet scan activity. It's going to light up, and it's going to be a false positive. They'd take that

00:00:58,610 --> 00:01:04,690
in consideration because it would be right at the scar or something like that. That's just a

00:01:04,930 --> 00:01:11,170
happen. Usually that calms down within a week or two, honestly. So I'd highly doubt that that's

00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:20,610
going to be the issue of this boy post surgery.

